Z||000000||fiero56||05-17-2000||05:48 PM||||Are the power mirrors on our Fieros the same for all five years. I was under the impression they are, but the Fiero Store has a pair listed as '86-'88. Whats going on here?<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-17-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-17-2000||09:06 PM||||The plugs are different and so are the motors themselves (at least they mount differently).  The earlier Fieros have white plugs and the later ('86-'88) have black plugs.  It really doesn't matter which one you use, as long as everything came from the same donor Fiero.  You can't "mix 'n match" components.    ||||reg||6
Z||000002||fiero56||05-18-2000||11:57 AM||||OK. Since I'm a little anal about correct era plugs on my car, I'll make sure I install '86-88 mirrors. There are no reliability differences between the two designs, right?<P>Hey Mike, check your e-mail. I sent you a message.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||05-18-2000||02:28 PM||||Yes you can mix and match. I have done it you just need to use a different connector and the plug is in the door and under the carpet so no matter how anal you are it will never matter what plug it has,||||reg||1
